# user data — never committed (local-first promise)
data/
.studyroom/
*.local.json
stats*.json

# measurement scratch — never committed, and the reason is not tidiness.
# `.scratch/` holds the wayfinder measurement runs, and those hold the owner's
# real material: 124 MB of her photographs under wayfinder-42/thumbs/, absolute
# /Users/ paths in every sample and fingerprint file, and OCR of her own notes.
# stage_public.py stages from `git ls-files`, so until 2026-08-13 the only thing
# keeping this off the public repo was that nobody had run `git add -A` — the
# directory was untracked but NOT ignored. Worse, the DENY gate reads text only
# (it skips on UnicodeDecodeError), so a paths file would have failed loudly
# while the photographs passed silently. Ignoring it is what makes the stager's
# tracked-files-only rule an actual guarantee instead of an accident.
# See wayfinder ticket #49 section 5.
.scratch/

